# UI/UX Pro Max (this repo)

Installed via `npx uipro-cli init --ai cursor`. Full workflow: **`.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md`**.

## Path fix (important)

Upstream examples use `skills/ui-ux-pro-max/...`. In Cursor installs, files live under **`.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/`**. From the repository root, run:

```bash
python .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<product + industry + keywords>" --design-system
```

Use `python3` on macOS/Linux if `python` is missing. On Windows, ensure Python is on PATH or use the `py` launcher.

## This project (Igloo Foretracker)

- Stack: **Next.js + Tailwind** — prefer **`--stack nextjs`** (and **`--stack shadcn`** if you adopt shadcn patterns) instead of the SKILL default `html-tailwind` when generating implementation guidance.
- For domain-specific UX detail: `--domain ux`, `--domain typography`, `--domain chart`, etc., as described in `SKILL.md`.

## When to activate

Use this skill for: new screens or flows, dashboard/analytics layout, landing/marketing visuals, color/typography decisions, chart choice, accessibility/visual review of UI, or explicit requests to “make it look professional / modern / on-brand.”

Combine with **`@frontend-developer`** or **`@ui-designer`** (Agency rules) when you need both the UUPM design system output and React/Next implementation discipline.
